## Define Compute Image for Provisioning

### Import Base OS Image

The following steps import the distribution installation media for use with
xCAT. A local copy of the distribution ISO is required; for this recipe the ISO
is `{{ distro_iso_image }}`. Initialize image creation using `copycds`, assuming
the ISO is available at `${iso_path}`:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Initialize OS images for use with xCAT -->
```bash
: "${iso_path:?ERROR: iso_path not set}"

copycds ${iso_path}/{{ distro_iso_image }}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

`copycds` derives the OS image names from the distribution metadata inside the
ISO, which encodes the minor version (for example a Rocky 10.0 x86_64 ISO
creates `rocky10.0-x86_64-{install,netboot,statelite}-compute`). Query the
created images and capture the stateful (*install*) image name for the
following steps:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Capture the install osimage name created by copycds -->
```bash
# Query available images
lsdef -t osimage

# Capture the stateful (install) compute image name
xcat_osimage=$(lsdef -t osimage | awk '/install-compute/{print $1; exit}')
echo ${xcat_osimage}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

The stateful install applies a default disk layout to the first detected disk
(a 1 GiB `/boot` plus an LVM volume group holding swap and a `/` volume grown
to fill the disk). Sites requiring a different layout can register a custom
partition file in kickstart syntax with
`chdef -t osimage ${xcat_osimage} partitionfile=<file>`; consult the
[xCAT documentation](https://xcat-docs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/) for details.

### Set Root Password for Compute Nodes

The kickstart generated for stateful installs reads the compute root password
from the xCAT `passwd` table, so the entry must exist before the provisioning
image is associated with the nodes. Administrative access relies on the head
node root ssh keys that xCAT installs during provisioning, so the randomly
generated password below is intentionally throwaway; sites that want
interactive (console) root logins should substitute a chosen password for the
`openssl rand` call. Store the password in crypted form:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Set root password used by the stateful install -->
```bash
chtab key=system passwd.username=root \
    passwd.password="$(openssl passwd -6 "$(openssl rand -base64 12)")"
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
